<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bad Gandersheim</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bad Gandersheim is a spa town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a>. It grew up around Gandersheim Abbey, founded in 852 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> count Liudolf and his wife Oda and moved there in 856, which as the family foundation of the Ottonian kings became a princely imperial abbey of noble canonesses. Its Romanesque abbey church survives, and an open-air <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> festival is held in front of it each summer.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bad-gandersheim.jpg" alt="Bad Gandersheim" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagar66 based on work of TUBS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bad_Gandersheim_in_NOM.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
